        "timestamp": 1778752388,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Taiwan says China 'sole risk' to peace after Xi warned Trump over Taiwan issue Asia / Pacific Issued on: 14/05/2026 - 11:53 It's an honor to be your friend - Donald Trump told Xi Jinping. Xi Jinping, however, responded by offering a cautionary warning about avoiding a possible clash between the two nations. A contrast in tone underscoring then just how far apart the leaders remain on thorny issues including the war in Iran, trade disputes and Washington’s relationship with Taiwan. Should Taiwan expect any substantive change in the US policy towards the island? Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Taipei, Jan Camenzind Broomby. Donald Trump and Xi Jinping hold high-stakes meeting in Beijing 14/05/2026 Asia / Pacific Taiwan vs China: Is conflict inevitable? 13/05/2026 Asia / Pacific Trump arrives in China for historic trip 13/05/2026 Asia / Pacific Trump 'could choose to change Taiwan policy in Beijing' unhindered by Congress, analyst says 12/05/2026 Asia / Pacific First US visit to China since 2017 amid geopolitical tension 12/05/2026 Asia / Pacific India: Modi wants Indians to stop buying gold 11/05/2026 Asia / Pacific At least 15 killed in car bomb attack on northwest Pakistan checkpoint 10/05/2026 Asia / Pacific At least three killed by volcano eruption in Indonesia 08/05/2026 Asia / Pacific China's 'key priorities': Open Hormuz, get oil flowing, avoid 'getting dragged into conflicts' 06/05/2026 Asia / Pacific"
